# Change
Recognized routed Claude compact requests now enter runtime semantic chunking above 95% of the smallest positive context_window/max_model_len, rather than waiting until above100%. The whole request estimator includes messages injected before request capping. Native Anthropic and ordinary opted-out turns retain their previous policy. Exactly95% remains passthrough; above95% chunks. Image-only encoded-size overflow still retains its conservative upstream handling.

# Verification
63 focused native passthrough, provider semantic compaction and context compaction tests passed in101.561s. New95/96 boundary regression checks minimum configured window and preflight opt-out. Existing failure/semantic budget coverage stayed green.

# Not yet proven
Read-only SSH on .14 confirms router9780 uses e208456. Logs show repeated muse compact failures at0/17 chunks, summary_calls1 with429 all credentials cooling down (Retry-After about342000s); chunk reduction cannot fix those failures. After model change,17:16:04 shows16/17 chunks, summary_calls17, saved_steps17, client_cancelled. Thus actual runtime chunking used17 sequential map calls, not just a native compact UI label.

Default map ceiling changed65536->131072, retaining half-budget bound, explicit smaller settings and rejection splitting. This is below previously failing261K segments, but successful production128K latency/stability is NOT yet proven. Regression checks fewer chunks with identical concatenated source projection, and smaller budget/config clamps.21 summary compatibility tests passed (1 pre-existing skip). No wall-clock speedup or exhausted credential recovery is claimed.
